<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index slightly firmer.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index slightly firmer.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index was 1.58 points, or 2.30 percent, higher at 70.39 after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index gained 52.62 points to 3,088.53.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 16.44 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Brothers, London newsroom +44 171 542 2734</p>
